---
/*
 * ============================================================================
 * src/pages/admin/editor.astro  —  the admin-only writing surface (Phase 4)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * WHAT THIS FILE IS / SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY
 * -----------------------------------------
 * The full in-browser authoring experience for the blog: a Medium-style
 * WYSIWYG editor plus the "Publish" flow that turns what you wrote into a
 * committed Markdown post. It is one Astro page — statically built like every
 * other route, but essentially a client-side app (all the logic lives in the
 * bottom <script>, which Astro bundles/transpiles). The page renders nothing
 * meaningful server-side beyond an empty shell + a hidden publish modal.
 *
 * WHERE IT SITS IN THE ARCHITECTURE
 * ---------------------------------
 * Stack: static Astro build hosted on Cloudflare Pages, with Pages Functions
 * (functions/api/*) for the few dynamic bits, Supabase for auth + data, and
 * Dodo for payments/premium (this page touches only auth + publish; it does
 * not talk to Dodo directly). Data flow when you hit Publish:
 *
 *   editor.astro (this file)                     ← author writes, gets Markdown
 *        │  POST /api/publish  { slug, content } + Supabase JWT (Bearer)
 *        ▼
 *   functions/api/publish.js (Pages Function)    ← re-verifies is_admin, then
 *        │  GitHub Contents API commit                commits src/content/blog/<slug>.md
 *        ▼
 *   GitHub repo → Cloudflare Pages Git build      ← rebuild redeploys the site
 *        ▼
 *   /blog/<slug>/  goes live (Astro content collection renders the .md)
 *
 * So this page never writes files itself and holds no repo credentials; it just
 * hands a Markdown blob + the user's JWT to the Function, which is the trusted
 * boundary. The published site renders the SAME fenced code (```d2 diagrams via
 * plugins/rehype-d2.mjs at build; ```python plots) so editor preview == live.
 *
 * KEY IMPORTS / DEPENDENCIES (see the <script> import block for the full list)
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *   - @milkdown/crepe                 the WYSIWYG editor ("Crepe" preset), Markdown-native
 *   - @milkdown/kit/prose/*           ProseMirror internals (Plugin/Decoration/…) for our
 *                                     two custom plugins: bracket auto-pairing + Plotly cells
 *   - @codemirror/language-data + /autocomplete   language-aware code blocks, close-brackets
 *   - @terrastruct/d2                 D2 diagram engine (WASM), lazy-loaded for ```d2 preview
 *   - ../../lib/plotly                runs author ```python via Pyodide + renders with plotly.js,
 *                                     plus makeRotatingGif() for 3D-figure GIF export
 *   - ../../lib/supabase             browser Supabase client (session, OAuth, magic-link, JWT)
 *   - ../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro  page chrome
 * WHAT DEPENDS ON THIS FILE: nothing imports it (it is a leaf route). It is the
 * sole producer of requests to functions/api/publish.js.
 *
 * IMPORTANT DESIGN DECISIONS / NON-OBVIOUS GOTCHAS
 * ------------------------------------------------
 *   - Markdown-native by design (Option B): Crepe serialises straight to the .md
 *     format the content collection consumes — no HTML round-trip, no lossy AST.
 *   - D2 REPLACED Mermaid. Diagrams are authored in ```d2 fences and previewed
 *     client-side via @terrastruct/d2 (see renderPreview below); the old Milkdown
 *     Mermaid plugin is gone. If you find "mermaid" anywhere, it is stale.
 *   - Interactive ```python plots are NOT drawn by Crepe's sanitised code-block
 *     preview. They are a separate ProseMirror WIDGET decoration (plotlyCells)
 *     injected just after each python block, so Plotly's interactivity/DOM
 *     survives Crepe's sanitiser. See the long comment on that plugin.
 *   - Two hand-rolled ProseMirror plugins are wired via crepe.editor.use():
 *     bracketPairing (auto-pair brackets/quotes in prose) and plotlyCells.
 *   - Draft autosave is localStorage-only for now (key 'aysr:editor-draft'),
 *     debounced; there is no server-side draft store yet (see the TODO).
 *   - The Publish modal is a two-state premium flow: sign-in view → metadata
 *     form. Frontmatter is built by hand and the leading "# Title" is stripped
 *     from the body to avoid a duplicate <h1> (title comes from frontmatter).
 *
 * SECURITY / CORRECTNESS CAVEATS  (READ BEFORE SHIPPING)
 * ------------------------------------------------------
 *   - !!! THE ADMIN GATE IS CURRENTLY DISABLED FOR DEV !!!  init() below has the
 *     session + is_admin() check commented out, so ANYONE can open this editor.
 *     That is intentional for building/testing without an admin login, but it
 *     MUST be restored before launch (the commented block shows exactly how).
 *     Even ungated, this is only UX exposure: the REAL protection is server-side
 *     at publish time — functions/api/publish.js re-verifies is_admin before it
 *     will commit anything, so a non-admin opening the editor still cannot ship.
 *   - Publish auth rides on the Supabase access_token sent as a Bearer header;
 *     the Function trusts that token, not the client's claims.
 *   - Frontmatter scalars are emitted via JSON.stringify (yaml() helper) because
 *     a JSON string literal is also a valid YAML scalar — this is the injection
 *     guard for user-supplied title/description/tags.
 * ============================================================================
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Editor — admin" description="Admin editor.">
  <p id="admin-gate" class="muted">Checking access…</p>

  <div id="editor-wrap" hidden>
    <div class="editor-bar">
      <strong>Draft</strong>
      <span id="editor-status" class="muted"></span>
      <button id="new-draft" type="button">New</button>
      <button id="get-md" type="button">Preview Markdown</button>
      <button id="publish-btn" type="button">Publish…</button>
    </div>
    <div id="publish-modal" class="pm-overlay" hidden>
      <div class="pm-card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Publish">
        <button class="pm-close" id="pm-close" type="button" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>

        <div id="pm-signin" hidden>
          <h2 class="pm-title">Sign in to publish</h2>
          <p class="pm-sub">Your draft is saved on this device. Sign in once to publish it to the world.</p>
          <button class="pm-btn pm-btn-primary" id="pm-github" type="button">Continue with GitHub</button>
          <div class="pm-or">or</div>
          <form id="pm-magic" class="pm-magic">
            <input id="pm-email" type="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required />
            <button class="pm-btn" type="submit">Email me a link</button>
          </form>
          <p class="pm-status" id="pm-signin-status"></p>
        </div>

        <div id="pm-form" hidden>
          <h2 class="pm-title">Ready to publish</h2>
          <label class="pm-field"><span class="pm-label">Title</span>
            <input id="pm-post-title" type="text" placeholder="Your title" /></label>
          <label class="pm-field"><span class="pm-label">Description</span>
            <textarea id="pm-post-desc" rows="2" placeholder="One sentence that makes people want to read."></textarea></label>
          <div class="pm-field"><span class="pm-label">Tags</span>
            <div class="pm-tags" id="pm-tags"><input id="pm-tag-input" type="text" placeholder="Add a tag…" /></div></div>
          <p class="pm-permalink">areyoustillreading.dev/blog/<span id="pm-slug" class="pm-slug" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false"></span></p>
          <label class="pm-toggle"><input id="pm-draft" type="checkbox" /> <span>Save as a draft — only you can see it</span></label>
          <div class="pm-actions">
            <button class="pm-btn pm-btn-primary" id="pm-publish" type="button">Publish</button>
            <span class="pm-status" id="pm-form-status"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="milkdown"></div>
    <pre id="md-out" hidden></pre>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .editor-bar {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 0.5rem 0; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .editor-bar button {
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--accent); color: #fff; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer;
  }
  #milkdown {
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; min-height: 60vh;
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  #md-out {
    margin-top: 1rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px; background: var(--code-bg); overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  /* The `hidden` attribute MUST win. Without this, the `.pm-overlay { display:flex }`
     rule below (author origin) overrides the UA `[hidden] { display:none }`, so the
     modal stays permanently rendered — an empty overlay covering the editor with a
     close button that appears dead (closeModal sets `hidden`, which display:flex
     ignores). This attribute-qualified selector has higher specificity, restoring it. */
  .pm-overlay[hidden] { display: none; }
  .pm-overlay {
    position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 100; display: flex; align-items: center;
    justify-content: center; padding: 1.5rem; background: rgba(12, 14, 18, 0.55);
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px); animation: pm-fade 0.15s ease;
  }
  @keyframes pm-fade { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }
  @keyframes pm-pop { from { transform: translateY(10px) scale(0.98); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
  .pm-card {
    position: relative; width: 100%; max-width: 30rem; background: var(--bg); color: inherit;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; padding: 2rem 2rem 1.75rem;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35); animation: pm-pop 0.18s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
  }
  .pm-close {
    position: absolute; top: 0.85rem; right: 1rem; border: 0; background: transparent;
    color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.7rem; line-height: 1; cursor: pointer; padding: 0;
  }
  .pm-title { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.45rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .pm-sub { margin: 0 0 1.35rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .pm-field { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .pm-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.07em; color: var(--muted); }
  .pm-card input[type="text"], .pm-card input[type="email"], .pm-card textarea {
    width: 100%; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font: inherit; color: inherit;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--code-bg, transparent);
  }
  .pm-card textarea { resize: vertical; line-height: 1.5; }
  .pm-card input:focus, .pm-card textarea:focus, .pm-slug:focus {
    outline: none; border-color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, transparent);
  }
  .pm-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: center; padding: 0.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; }
  .pm-tags input { flex: 1; min-width: 6rem; border: 0 !important; padding: 0.25rem 0.35rem !important; background: transparent !important; box-shadow: none !important; }
  .pm-chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.85em; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent); }
  .pm-chip button { border: 0; background: transparent; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1; cursor: pointer; padding: 0; }
  .pm-permalink { margin: 0.1rem 0 1.1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .pm-slug { color: var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 0.15rem; outline: none; }
  .pm-toggle { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; margin-bottom: 1.35rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); cursor: pointer; }
  .pm-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; }
  .pm-btn { padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; background: transparent; color: inherit; font: inherit; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; }
  .pm-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: default; }
  .pm-btn-primary { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
  #pm-signin .pm-btn-primary { width: 100%; }
  #pm-form .pm-btn-primary { padding-inline: 1.6rem; }
  .pm-or { margin: 0.9rem 0; text-align: center; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .pm-magic { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .pm-magic input { flex: 1; }
  .pm-status { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>

<!-- Global (unscoped) styles: the code-block preview DOM is created by Milkdown at
     runtime, so Astro's scoped styles never reach it — target these classes globally. -->
<style is:global>
  .d2-preview { display: flex; justify-content: center; padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  .d2-preview svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .d2-error {
    padding: 1rem; color: #e5484d; white-space: pre-wrap;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .plotly-cell { margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: hidden; }
  .plotly-holder { width: 100%; height: 380px; }
  .py-running { padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem; opacity: 0.6; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .py-output {
    margin: 0; padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--code-bg); border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .plotly-error {
    padding: 0.75rem; margin: 0; color: #e5484d; white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-x: auto; font-size: 0.85em;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .plotly-controls {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .plotly-controls .pc-label { font-weight: 600; opacity: 0.85; }
  .plotly-controls label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.25rem; opacity: 0.85; }
  .plotly-controls input {
    width: 3.5rem; padding: 0.15rem 0.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px; background: var(--bg); color: inherit;
  }
  /* !important: the Milkdown/Crepe editor theme otherwise overrides editor buttons
     to a transparent background, making this one invisible (white text on white). */
  .plotly-controls button {
    padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem !important; border: 0 !important; border-radius: 6px !important;
    background: var(--accent) !important; color: #fff !important; opacity: 1 !important;
    font-weight: 600 !important; font-size: 0.85em !important; cursor: pointer !important;
  }
  .plotly-controls button:disabled { opacity: 0.55 !important; cursor: default !important; }
  .plotly-controls .pc-status { opacity: 0.75; }
</style>

<script>
  import { supabase } from '../../lib/supabase';
  import { Crepe } from '@milkdown/crepe';
  import { languages } from '@codemirror/language-data';
  import { closeBrackets, closeBracketsKeymap } from '@codemirror/autocomplete';
  import { keymap } from '@codemirror/view';
  import { $prose } from '@milkdown/kit/utils';
  import { Plugin, PluginKey, TextSelection } from '@milkdown/kit/prose/state';
  import { Decoration, DecorationSet } from '@milkdown/kit/prose/view';
  import { renderPlotlyFigure, loadPlotlyJs, makeRotatingGif } from '../../lib/plotly';
  import '@milkdown/crepe/theme/common/style.css';
  import '@milkdown/crepe/theme/nord.css';

  // Auto-pair brackets AND quotes across the whole editor (blog-wide, prose side).
  // Typing an opener inserts its closer with the cursor between (e.g. '(|)'); typing
  // a closer/quote that's already next "types over" it; Backspace on an empty pair
  // deletes both. Code blocks get the same behavior via CodeMirror's closeBrackets.
  // NOTE: backtick is deliberately NOT paired here — it collides with Markdown's own
  // inline-code and fenced-code-block (```) shortcuts, which Milkdown handles natively.
  const PAIRS = { '(': ')', '[': ']', '{': '}', '"': '"', "'": "'" };
  const CLOSERS = new Set([')', ']', '}']);
  const QUOTES = new Set(['"', "'"]);

  const bracketPairing = $prose(() => new Plugin({
    props: {
      handleTextInput(view, from, to, text) {
        const { state } = view;
        const closing = PAIRS[text];
        if (closing) {
          if (QUOTES.has(text) && from === to) {
            // Type over an existing identical quote instead of nesting a new pair.
            if (state.doc.textBetween(from, from + 1) === text) {
              view.dispatch(state.tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(state.doc, from + 1)));
              return true;
            }
            // Don't auto-pair a quote right after a word char (contractions: don't, it's).
            const before = from > 0 ? state.doc.textBetween(from - 1, from) : '';
            if (/\w/.test(before)) return false;
          }
          const tr = state.tr;
          if (from !== to) {
            // Wrap the current selection in the pair, keeping it selected.
            const inner = state.doc.textBetween(from, to);
            tr.insertText(text + inner + closing, from, to);
            tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(tr.doc, from + 1, from + 1 + inner.length));
          } else {
            tr.insertText(text + closing, from, to);
            tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(tr.doc, from + 1));
          }
          view.dispatch(tr);
          return true;
        }
        // Type over a bracket closer that's already the next character.
        if (CLOSERS.has(text) && from === to && state.doc.textBetween(from, from + 1) === text) {
          view.dispatch(state.tr.setSelection(TextSelection.create(state.doc, from + 1)));
          return true;
        }
        return false;
      },
      handleKeyDown(view, event) {
        if (event.key !== 'Backspace') return false;
        const { state } = view;
        const sel = state.selection;
        if (!sel.empty || sel.from === 0) return false;
        const before = state.doc.textBetween(sel.from - 1, sel.from);
        const after = state.doc.textBetween(sel.from, sel.from + 1);
        // Cursor sits between an empty pair -> delete both sides.
        if (PAIRS[before] && PAIRS[before] === after) {
          view.dispatch(state.tr.delete(sel.from - 1, sel.from + 1));
          return true;
        }
        return false;
      },
    },
  }));

  // Lazy-load D2 (@terrastruct/d2, WASM) only when a ```d2 diagram is first
  // previewed, then reuse the one instance. Kept out of the initial editor bundle
  // via import(). The published site renders the same fences at build time
  // (plugins/rehype-d2), so editor preview and live output match.
  let d2Promise = null;
  function loadD2() {
    if (!d2Promise) d2Promise = import('@terrastruct/d2').then(({ D2 }) => new D2());
    return d2Promise;
  }
  async function renderD2(code) {
    const d2 = await loadD2();
    const res = await d2.compile(code, { pad: 20, noXMLTag: true });
    return await d2.render(res.diagram, res.renderOptions);
  }
  function diagramEl(svg) {
    const el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'd2-preview';
    el.innerHTML = svg;
    return el;
  }
  function errorEl(err) {
    const el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'd2-error';
    el.textContent = 'D2 error: ' + (err && err.message ? err.message : String(err));
    return el;
  }

  // --- Interactive Python plot cells (Plotly) ---------------------------------
  // Each ```python block gets a live, interactive plot rendered right below it —
  // a notebook-style cell. The author's plotly.py runs client-side via Pyodide
  // (lib/plotly) and plotly.js renders the figure, so 3D plots rotate/zoom right
  // in the editor. The panel is a ProseMirror WIDGET decoration (non-editable,
  // outside Crepe's sanitizer) so interactivity survives. Panels are keyed by the
  // python block's index, so a panel (and its plot) persists while you edit —
  // only its contents re-render, debounced.
  const plotlyKey = new PluginKey('plotly-cells');

  const plotlyCells = $prose(() => {
    const panels = new Map(); // key -> panel DOM
    const timers = new Map(); // panel -> debounce timer id
    let plotlyJs = null;

    function render(panel, code) {
      if (panel.__code === code) return;
      panel.__code = code;
      clearTimeout(timers.get(panel));
      if (!code) { panel.replaceChildren(); panel.__ran = false; return; }
      // Show "Running…" only before a cell's FIRST result; later edits keep the last
      // output visible until the new one is ready (no flicker/spam while typing).
      if (!panel.__ran) {
        const s = document.createElement('div');
        s.className = 'py-running';
        s.textContent = 'Running…';
        panel.replaceChildren(s);
      }
      timers.set(panel, setTimeout(async () => {
        let res;
        try {
          res = await renderPlotlyFigure(code);
        } catch (e) {
          res = { error: 'Could not run: ' + (e && e.message ? e.message : String(e)) };
        }
        if (panel.__code !== code) return; // superseded by a newer edit
        panel.__ran = true;
        const { figure, stdout, error } = res;
        if (error) {
          const pre = document.createElement('pre');
          pre.className = 'plotly-error';
          pre.textContent = error;
          panel.replaceChildren(pre);
        } else if (figure) {
          // Plotting cell -> interactive plot.
          if (!plotlyJs) plotlyJs = await loadPlotlyJs();
          let holder = panel.querySelector('.plotly-holder');
          if (!holder) {
            holder = document.createElement('div');
            holder.className = 'plotly-holder';
            panel.replaceChildren(holder);
          }
          // Fit the plot to the editor column: drop any hard-coded width/height the
          // figure set (e.g. width=800) so it can't overflow; autosize to the holder.
          const layout = { ...(figure.layout || {}) };
          delete layout.width;
          delete layout.height;
          layout.autosize = true;
          await plotlyJs.react(holder, figure.data || [], layout, { responsive: true, displaylogo: false });
          requestAnimationFrame(() => { try { plotlyJs.Plots.resize(holder); } catch {} });
          updateControls(panel, holder, figure);
        } else {
          // Non-plotting cell -> a notebook-style output block showing stdout. If the
          // cell printed nothing, show nothing (no clutter).
          const out = (stdout || '').replace(/\s+$/, '');
          if (out) {
            const pre = document.createElement('pre');
            pre.className = 'py-output';
            pre.textContent = out;
            panel.replaceChildren(pre);
          } else {
            panel.replaceChildren();
          }
        }
      }, 700));
    }

    // For 3D figures, offer a rotating-GIF export below the plot (author sets the
    // frame count and fps). 2D figures get no controls.
    function updateControls(panel, holder, figure) {
      const types = (figure.data || []).map((t) => t && t.type).filter(Boolean);
      const is3d = !!(figure.layout && figure.layout.scene) ||
        types.some((t) => /3d$/.test(t) || ['surface', 'mesh3d', 'cone', 'streamtube', 'volume', 'isosurface'].includes(t));
      let bar = panel.querySelector('.plotly-controls');
      if (!is3d) { if (bar) bar.remove(); return; }
      if (bar) return; // already present
      bar = document.createElement('div');
      bar.className = 'plotly-controls';
      bar.innerHTML =
        '<span class="pc-label">Rotating GIF</span>' +
        '<label>frames <input type="number" class="pc-frames" value="36" min="4" max="180"></label>' +
        '<label>fps <input type="number" class="pc-fps" value="15" min="1" max="60"></label>' +
        '<button type="button" class="pc-gif">Download GIF</button>' +
        '<span class="pc-status"></span>';
      const btn = bar.querySelector('.pc-gif');
      const status = bar.querySelector('.pc-status');
      btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const frames = Math.max(4, Math.min(180, parseInt(bar.querySelector('.pc-frames').value, 10) || 36));
        const fps = Math.max(1, Math.min(60, parseInt(bar.querySelector('.pc-fps').value, 10) || 15));
        btn.disabled = true;
        status.textContent = 'Rendering… 0%';
        try {
          const blob = await makeRotatingGif(holder, {
            frames, fps,
            onProgress: (p) => { status.textContent = 'Rendering… ' + Math.round(p * 100) + '%'; },
          });
          const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
          const a = document.createElement('a');
          a.href = url;
          a.download = 'plot.gif';
          document.body.appendChild(a);
          a.click();
          a.remove();
          URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
          status.textContent = 'Saved · ' + Math.round(blob.size / 1024) + ' KB';
        } catch (e) {
          status.textContent = 'Failed: ' + (e && e.message ? e.message : String(e));
        } finally {
          btn.disabled = false;
        }
      });
      panel.appendChild(bar);
    }

    function build(state) {
      const decos = [];
      const used = new Set();
      let i = 0;
      state.doc.descendants((node, pos) => {
        if (node.type.name !== 'code_block') return;
        const lang = (node.attrs.language || '').toLowerCase();
        if (lang !== 'python' && lang !== 'py') return;
        const key = 'py-' + i++;
        used.add(key);
        let panel = panels.get(key);
        if (!panel) {
          panel = document.createElement('div');
          panel.className = 'plotly-cell';
          panels.set(key, panel);
        }
        render(panel, node.textContent.trim());
        decos.push(Decoration.widget(pos + node.nodeSize, panel, {
          key, side: 1, ignoreSelection: true, stopEvent: () => true,
        }));
      });
      // Drop panels whose block was removed.
      for (const [k, p] of panels) {
        if (!used.has(k)) {
          clearTimeout(timers.get(p));
          timers.delete(p);
          if (plotlyJs) { try { plotlyJs.purge(p.querySelector('.plotly-holder')); } catch {} }
          panels.delete(k);
        }
      }
      return DecorationSet.create(state.doc, decos);
    }

    return new Plugin({
      key: plotlyKey,
      state: {
        init: (_, state) => build(state),
        apply: (tr, old, _o, newState) => (tr.docChanged ? build(newState) : old),
      },
      props: { decorations(state) { return plotlyKey.getState(state); } },
    });
  });

  const gate = document.getElementById('admin-gate');
  const wrap = document.getElementById('editor-wrap');
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('editor-status');

  async function init() {
    // TEMP (dev): the editor is intentionally UNGATED so it can be built and tested
    // from a general user's POV without an admin login. BEFORE LAUNCH, restore the
    // gate here — require a session AND is_admin:
    //   const { data } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
    //   if (!data.session) { gate.innerHTML = 'Please <a href="/login">sign in</a> to write.'; return; }
    //   const { data: a } = await supabase.rpc('is_admin');
    //   if (a !== true) { gate.textContent = 'Admins only.'; return; }
    gate.hidden = true;
    wrap.hidden = false;

    // Draft persistence (dev): autosave the Markdown to localStorage so work survives
    // reloads. TODO: migrate to per-user Supabase drafts once the editor is re-gated.
    const DRAFT_KEY = 'aysr:editor-draft';
    let savedDraft = null;
    try { savedDraft = localStorage.getItem(DRAFT_KEY); } catch {}

    const crepe = new Crepe({
      root: document.getElementById('milkdown'),
      defaultValue: savedDraft != null ? savedDraft : '# New post\n\nStart writing.\n',
      featureConfigs: {
        // Language-aware code blocks: hand the CodeMirror feature the full
        // language set (from @codemirror/language-data) so a block tagged ts /
        // python / rust / etc. loads that grammar and highlights accordingly,
        // with a language picker in the block. Matches the build-time Shiki output.
        [Crepe.Feature.CodeMirror]: {
          languages,
          // Auto-close brackets/quotes: typing '(' inserts '()' with the cursor
          // between (i.e. '(|)'), and Backspace on the empty pair removes BOTH.
          extensions: [closeBrackets(), keymap.of(closeBracketsKeymap)],
          // Live diagrams: for a ```d2 block, render it client-side (D2 WASM) into
          // the block's preview panel (a toggle appears in the block's toolbar).
          // undefined return = async; applyPreview() swaps in the SVG when ready.
          // Any other language returns null -> no preview toggle, no overhead. On
          // publish the same ```d2 fence is rendered at build time by
          // plugins/rehype-d2, so editor preview and live site stay identical.
          renderPreview: (language, content, applyPreview) => {
            const lang = (language || '').toLowerCase();
            const code = content.trim();
            if (!code) return null;
            if (lang === 'd2') {
              renderD2(code)
                .then((svg) => applyPreview(diagramEl(svg)))
                .catch((err) => applyPreview(errorEl(err)));
              return undefined;
            }
            // Python plots are handled by the interactive Plotly panel plugin
            // (rendered below the block), not by this sanitized preview.
            return null;
          },
          previewLabel: 'Diagram',
        },
      },
    });
    let saveTimer = null;
    crepe.on((api) => {
      api.markdownUpdated((_ctx, md) => {
        statusEl.textContent = 'Saving…';
        clearTimeout(saveTimer);
        saveTimer = setTimeout(() => {
          try { localStorage.setItem(DRAFT_KEY, md); statusEl.textContent = 'Saved'; }
          catch { statusEl.textContent = 'Save failed'; }
        }, 800);
      });
    });

    crepe.editor.use(bracketPairing);
    crepe.editor.use(plotlyCells);
    await crepe.create();
    if (savedDraft != null) statusEl.textContent = 'Draft restored';

    // "New" clears the saved draft and starts a fresh post (two-click confirm so an
    // accidental click can't nuke your work).
    let armNew = false;
    const newBtn = document.getElementById('new-draft');
    newBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!armNew) {
        armNew = true;
        newBtn.textContent = 'Confirm New?';
        setTimeout(() => { armNew = false; newBtn.textContent = 'New'; }, 3000);
        return;
      }
      try { localStorage.removeItem(DRAFT_KEY); } catch {}
      location.reload();
    });

    // "Preview Markdown" shows the serialized Markdown (temporary debug view — this
    // is what Publish will commit to GitHub in the next increment).
    const out = document.getElementById('md-out');
    document.getElementById('get-md').addEventListener('click', () => {
      out.hidden = false;
      out.textContent = crepe.getMarkdown();
    });

    // --- Publish (premium modal) --------------------------------------------
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const modal = $('publish-modal');
    const slugify = (s) => s.toLowerCase().trim().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '').slice(0, 80);
    const firstHeading = (md) => { const m = md.match(/^#\s+(.+)$/m); return m ? m[1].trim() : ''; };
    const yaml = (v) => JSON.stringify(String(v == null ? '' : v)); // JSON-style scalar is valid YAML
    let pubTags = [];
    let slugEdited = false;

    const openModal = () => {
      modal.hidden = false;
      // Show the sign-in view immediately so the card is never blank while the async
      // session check runs; refreshAuthView() swaps to the form if already signed in.
      $('pm-signin').hidden = false;
      $('pm-form').hidden = true;
      refreshAuthView();
    };
    const closeModal = () => { modal.hidden = true; };
    $('publish-btn').addEventListener('click', openModal);
    $('pm-close').addEventListener('click', closeModal);
    modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if (e.target === modal) closeModal(); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Escape' && !modal.hidden) closeModal(); });

    // Decide which of the two modal views to show. INVARIANT: exactly one of
    // #pm-signin / #pm-form is visible at all times — the card must NEVER render
    // empty (both hidden). Every failure mode below falls back to the sign-in
    // view, so a thrown/hung/blocked session check (corrupt localStorage token, a
    // privacy extension blocking Supabase, an offline refresh, etc.) can only ever
    // land on "Sign in to publish", not a blank card.
    async function refreshAuthView() {
      let signedIn = false;
      try {
        // Guard against a hang: getSession() can await a background token refresh,
        // and if that network call is blocked it never resolves. Cap it so the UI
        // always settles instead of leaving whatever view was up.
        const withTimeout = Promise.race([
          supabase.auth.getSession(),
          new Promise((res) => setTimeout(() => res({ data: { session: null }, __timedOut: true }), 4000)),
        ]);
        const { data } = await withTimeout;
        signedIn = !!(data && data.session && data.session.user);
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('[publish] session check failed; falling back to sign-in view', err);
        signedIn = false;
      }
      $('pm-signin').hidden = signedIn;
      $('pm-form').hidden = !signedIn;
      if (signedIn) { try { prefillForm(); } catch (err) { console.error('[publish] prefill failed', err); } }
    }
    function prefillForm() {
      if (!$('pm-post-title').value) $('pm-post-title').value = firstHeading(crepe.getMarkdown());
      if (!$('pm-slug').textContent.trim()) $('pm-slug').textContent = slugify($('pm-post-title').value);
    }
    // Keep the permalink synced to the title until the author edits it directly.
    $('pm-slug').addEventListener('input', () => { slugEdited = true; });
    $('pm-post-title').addEventListener('input', () => { if (!slugEdited) $('pm-slug').textContent = slugify($('pm-post-title').value); });

    // Sign-in (one-time; the session persists after).
    $('pm-github').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      $('pm-signin-status').textContent = 'Redirecting to GitHub…';
      await supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'github', options: { redirectTo: location.href } });
    });
    $('pm-magic').addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const email = $('pm-email').value.trim();
      if (!email) return;
      $('pm-signin-status').textContent = 'Sending…';
      const { error } = await supabase.auth.signInWithOtp({ email, options: { emailRedirectTo: location.href } });
      $('pm-signin-status').textContent = error ? ('Error: ' + error.message) : 'Check your inbox for the magic link.';
    });
    supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange(() => { if (!modal.hidden) refreshAuthView(); });

    // Tags as chips.
    const tagInput = $('pm-tag-input');
    function renderTags() {
      $('pm-tags').querySelectorAll('.pm-chip').forEach((c) => c.remove());
      pubTags.forEach((t, i) => {
        const chip = document.createElement('span');
        chip.className = 'pm-chip';
        chip.textContent = t;
        const x = document.createElement('button');
        x.type = 'button';
        x.textContent = '×';
        x.addEventListener('click', () => { pubTags.splice(i, 1); renderTags(); });
        chip.appendChild(x);
        $('pm-tags').insertBefore(chip, tagInput);
      });
    }
    tagInput.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if ((e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ',') && tagInput.value.trim()) {
        e.preventDefault();
        const t = tagInput.value.trim().replace(/,+$/, '');
        if (t && !pubTags.includes(t) && pubTags.length < 5) pubTags.push(t);
        tagInput.value = '';
        renderTags();
      } else if (e.key === 'Backspace' && !tagInput.value && pubTags.length) {
        pubTags.pop();
        renderTags();
      }
    });

    // Publish.
    $('pm-publish').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const status = $('pm-form-status');
      const title = $('pm-post-title').value.trim();
      const description = $('pm-post-desc').value.trim();
      const slug = slugify($('pm-slug').textContent || title);
      const draft = $('pm-draft').checked;
      if (!title) return void (status.textContent = 'Add a title.');
      if (!description) return void (status.textContent = 'Add a description.');
      if (!slug) return void (status.textContent = 'Need a permalink.');
      const { data } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
      const token = data.session && data.session.access_token;
      if (!token) { status.textContent = 'Please sign in again.'; refreshAuthView(); return; }

      // Title lives in frontmatter (rendered as the page <h1>), so drop a leading
      // "# Title" from the body to avoid a duplicate heading.
      const body = crepe.getMarkdown().replace(/^#\s+.+\n+/, '');
      const today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
      const content = [
        '---',
        `title: ${yaml(title)}`,
        `description: ${yaml(description)}`,
        `pubDate: ${yaml(today)}`,
        `tags: [${pubTags.map(yaml).join(', ')}]`,
        `draft: ${draft}`,
        '---',
        '',
      ].join('\n') + body;

      status.textContent = 'Publishing…';
      $('pm-publish').disabled = true;
      // Set once publish succeeds and we begin waiting for the rebuild, so the `finally`
      // below doesn't re-enable the button while we're about to navigate away.
      let navigating = false;
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/publish', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', Authorization: 'Bearer ' + token },
          body: JSON.stringify({ slug, content }),
        });
        const j = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
        if (res.ok && j.ok) {
          navigating = true;
          // Publishing is a git commit that triggers a fresh site build (~1-2 min); the
          // post's page does not exist until that build finishes. Rather than leave the
          // author on a "rebuilding" note (and a link that 404s until then), poll the
          // post URL and navigate to it the instant it goes live — so submitting the
          // form lands them on their real, published post.
          const postUrl = '/blog/' + slug + '/';
          status.textContent = (j.updated ? 'Updated' : 'Published') + ' — building your post… (~1–2 min)';
          const deadline = Date.now() + 5 * 60 * 1000;
          const goWhenLive = async () => {
            if (modal.hidden) return; // author closed the modal → they opted out of the auto-jump
            try {
              // Cache-bust + no-store so we see the fresh deployment, not an edge-cached 404.
              const r = await fetch(postUrl + '?_=' + Date.now(), { cache: 'no-store' });
              if (r.ok) { status.textContent = "It's live — taking you there…"; location.href = postUrl; return; }
            } catch { /* transient during rollout — keep polling */ }
            if (Date.now() < deadline) { setTimeout(goWhenLive, 4000); return; }
            // Build ran unusually long — hand back a manual link instead of hanging.
            navigating = false;
            $('pm-publish').disabled = false;
            status.innerHTML = 'Published — still building. <a href="' + postUrl + '">Open it →</a>';
          };
          setTimeout(goWhenLive, 5000);
        } else {
          status.textContent = "Couldn't publish: " + (j.error || ('HTTP ' + res.status));
        }
      } catch (e) {
        status.textContent = 'Error: ' + (e && e.message ? e.message : String(e));
      } finally {
        if (!navigating) $('pm-publish').disabled = false;
      }
    });
  }

  init();
</script>
